WEBVTT

00:00:05.530 --> 00:00:08.730
<i>It consumes all, drowning 
anyone who challenges it...</i>

00:00:08.730 --> 00:00:11.990
<i>The devil known as the Bog!</i>

00:00:12.450 --> 00:00:16.490
<i>Taking it on is the man of legend: Itou Kaiji!</i>

00:00:16.910 --> 00:00:21.130
<i>Opposing him alongside the Bog is 
the manager of its casino, Ichijou!</i>

00:00:21.130 --> 00:00:23.680
<i>A cunning venomous snake!</i>

00:00:23.680 --> 00:00:25.510
I may as well watch it end...

00:00:26.290 --> 00:00:29.000
The conclusion to your dream. Your last gasp.

00:00:33.560 --> 00:00:37.220
<i>We now turn time backward 
from that legendary evening...</i>

00:00:37.220 --> 00:00:43.230
<i>Tonight, a certain man will battle 
with the Bog long before Kaiji does.</i>

00:00:43.230 --> 00:00:46.090
I'm sure you're already aware of this,

00:00:46.090 --> 00:00:50.230
but we're currently headed to an underground 
casino owned by the Teiai Group.

00:00:50.580 --> 00:00:54.480
The man you'll be taking on there is

00:00:54.480 --> 00:00:59.370
the unbeatable Bog, known as 
the demonic pachinko machine.

00:01:00.180 --> 00:01:04.240
It has consumed the balls of 
countless players up to now.

00:01:04.240 --> 00:01:07.120
The jackpot is currently 
worth 1.5 billion yen.

00:01:07.120 --> 00:01:12.150
It'd be wonderful if you were able to collect 
the 1.5 billion today, Tonegawa-sensei.

00:01:12.150 --> 00:01:14.630
I get it. Basically...

00:01:15.020 --> 00:01:16.370
it's rigged, right?

00:01:17.830 --> 00:01:22.370
An event for collecting the 1.5 billion with 
a rigged game to entertain a Teiai exec...

00:01:23.800 --> 00:01:26.420
I'll gladly humor you.

00:01:31.570 --> 00:01:38.120
<b>Middle Management Blues</b>

00:01:31.570 --> 00:01:38.120
<b><i>Mr. Tonegawa</i></b>

00:02:59.130 --> 00:03:03.050
It's an honor to have you, Tonegawa-sensei.

00:03:00.240 --> 00:03:03.820
<i>Agenda 20
<b></b></i>\h\h\h\h\h\hEntertaining

00:03:03.050 --> 00:03:04.880
We've been waiting.

00:03:04.880 --> 00:03:08.910
I am the manager of this casino, 
and my name is Icihijou.

00:03:10.100 --> 00:03:13.540
I'm sure you're already aware,

00:03:13.540 --> 00:03:15.540
but if I'm being quite frank,

00:03:15.540 --> 00:03:17.550
we are here to amuse you.

00:03:17.870 --> 00:03:19.290
You are a guest...

00:03:19.290 --> 00:03:23.450
Rather, a Teiai Group executive. 
To go even further,

00:03:23.450 --> 00:03:26.360
you are the man known as number 
two in the Teiai Group,

00:03:26.360 --> 00:03:28.680
and you are here to win the jackpot!

00:03:26.360 --> 00:03:28.680
<i>This guy talks a lot.</i>

00:03:28.680 --> 00:03:32.550
This casino is here for your convenience.

00:03:28.890 --> 00:03:34.190
<b>Blabber... Blabber...</b>

00:03:31.530 --> 00:03:33.120
<i>He doesn't know when to quit.</i>

00:03:33.120 --> 00:03:34.940
But in spite of that,

00:03:34.940 --> 00:03:40.190
we will not be showing you a bit, 
not even the slightest shred, of mercy!

00:03:39.440 --> 00:03:40.190
<b>Psst...</b>

00:03:40.630 --> 00:03:42.160
That won't be a problem, will it?

00:03:42.160 --> 00:03:43.320
<i>Psst...</i>

00:03:43.320 --> 00:03:45.610
Considering that you are the man known as

00:03:45.610 --> 00:03:48.950
Teiai's number two, 
the brilliant Tonegawa-sensei.

00:03:50.360 --> 00:03:53.000
<i>I see. This brat...</i>

00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:57.220
<i>He's more of a viper than he looks.</i>

00:03:58.120 --> 00:03:58.960
<i>Very well.</i>

00:03:59.370 --> 00:04:01.460
<i>It'd be boring otherwise.</i>

00:04:02.260 --> 00:04:03.720
But, boss...

00:04:04.850 --> 00:04:06.470
Whisper, whisper, whisper...

00:04:06.470 --> 00:04:09.090
What?! You're sure about that?!

00:04:09.090 --> 00:04:09.890
Yes, sir.

00:04:11.290 --> 00:04:13.230
I should've expected it from a Teiai exec...

00:04:13.230 --> 00:04:16.980
No, the one known as the 
company's number two man!

00:04:18.490 --> 00:04:19.780
By pure coincidence,

00:04:19.780 --> 00:04:23.360
the pins today are set to the 
configuration that is worst for us.

00:04:23.360 --> 00:04:24.830
They are?

00:04:24.830 --> 00:04:26.990
Yes. Our Bog...

00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:31.260
normally has three different 
daily settings: A, B, and C.

00:04:31.260 --> 00:04:32.250
There's C...

00:04:32.250 --> 00:04:37.280
Under that setting, one out of a hundred 
balls will make its way through.

00:04:37.280 --> 00:04:38.500
Then comes B.

00:04:38.500 --> 00:04:43.010
With it, one out of sixty 
balls will clear the pins.

00:04:43.010 --> 00:04:44.760
Then there's A,

00:04:44.760 --> 00:04:49.430
in which one out of thirty balls is able 
to make its way to the flippers.

00:04:49.430 --> 00:04:51.990
But the day that we're hosting you...

00:04:51.990 --> 00:04:56.290
I had thought it would be on 
the semi-monthly A setting, but...

00:04:57.000 --> 00:04:58.520
Of all the days for this!

00:04:58.520 --> 00:05:02.220
Of all the days... Of all the days...

00:05:02.220 --> 00:05:04.410
It's the once-in-five-years setting,

00:05:04.410 --> 00:05:06.780
setting Y!

00:05:09.000 --> 00:05:10.030
<i>Y!</i>

00:05:09.730 --> 00:05:15.600
<i>Y... Y... Y...</i>

00:05:10.710 --> 00:05:15.570
I see... It seems you truly 
have the devil's own luck.

00:05:15.570 --> 00:05:16.610
Well, that's that.

00:05:16.610 --> 00:05:19.920
We'll simply have to face 
you under the Y settings.

00:05:20.230 --> 00:05:21.670
Expect no mercy!

00:05:24.090 --> 00:05:24.920
<i>It begins...</i>

00:05:25.590 --> 00:05:29.430
<i>Manager Ichijou's diabolical reception!</i>

00:05:32.170 --> 00:05:35.020
<i>Tonegawa fires away!</i>

00:05:35.020 --> 00:05:38.060
<i>The first challenge in his 
way is the forest of pins.</i>

00:05:39.330 --> 00:05:41.250
<i>With ordinary settings, in this challenge,</i>

00:05:41.250 --> 00:05:44.570
<i>the best case scenario would see one 
in thirty balls make its way through.</i>

00:05:44.570 --> 00:05:49.430
<i>But today is the one-in-five-years 
setting of Y!</i>

00:05:49.430 --> 00:05:52.580
<i>Inevitably, nine out of ten 
balls are beckoned through!</i>

00:05:53.810 --> 00:05:56.070
I knew this setting would have this effect...

00:05:56.070 --> 00:05:57.870
But it's not over yet!

00:05:58.930 --> 00:06:03.140
<i>Next are the flippers that 
will randomly block balls.</i>

00:06:03.560 --> 00:06:05.880
<i>Countless challengers have been bested</i>

00:06:05.880 --> 00:06:09.800
<i>by this capricious gatekeeper, 
and left suffering!</i>

00:06:12.130 --> 00:06:15.350
You won't find this next 
part quite so simple!

00:06:15.350 --> 00:06:17.910
<i>But things are different today.</i>

00:06:17.910 --> 00:06:22.190
<i>The moment the sensors sense a ball passing 
through the pins, it's programmed to open!</i>

00:06:24.870 --> 00:06:27.950
<i>It lies in wait, like a starving beast!</i>

00:06:28.290 --> 00:06:30.240
<i>With its mouth wide open!</i>

00:06:30.240 --> 00:06:32.950
<i>No way out! The balls cannot escape!</i>

00:06:35.990 --> 00:06:38.000
How is this possible?!

00:06:41.480 --> 00:06:45.000
<i>Before he knows it, he's waist-deep 
in the middle of the bog!</i>

00:06:47.690 --> 00:06:50.360
He made it to the plates already!

00:06:50.360 --> 00:06:52.890
To think it could be so simple!

00:06:54.370 --> 00:06:57.750
I-I suppose I should have expected as 
much from Teiai's number two man.

00:06:57.750 --> 00:07:00.520
In the face of the challenge 
the Bog presents...

00:07:00.520 --> 00:07:03.700
He's barely even fazed! It's terrifying!

00:07:03.700 --> 00:07:05.520
What a fearsome man!

00:07:06.010 --> 00:07:07.960
<i>I'm absolutely positive.</i>

00:07:07.960 --> 00:07:12.170
<i>This Ichijou has no idea 
how to entertain a guest.</i>

00:07:17.010 --> 00:07:21.320
<i>Whatever the game, if you're 
offering it to entertain a guest,</i>

00:07:21.320 --> 00:07:24.470
<i>the point is to make your 
skills appear roughly even</i>

00:07:24.930 --> 00:07:28.810
<i>in order to increase your 
opponent's excitement.</i>

00:07:33.480 --> 00:07:36.050
<i>And then, at the very end,</i>

00:07:36.970 --> 00:07:38.970
<i>you lose by the slimmest of margins.</i>

00:07:39.440 --> 00:07:43.600
<i>That's how you leave them 
feeling the most satisfied.</i>

00:07:44.330 --> 00:07:48.110
<i>But this kid's method is pathetically obvious.</i>

00:07:48.570 --> 00:07:51.860
<i>He's putting on the airs of 
a tooth and nail struggle,</i>

00:07:51.860 --> 00:07:55.120
<i>but in reality, he's got kid gloves on.</i>

00:07:55.120 --> 00:07:57.110
He's a demon! A dark prince!

00:07:57.110 --> 00:07:59.350
No, a gambling monster!

00:07:59.350 --> 00:08:02.870
Have you come to take down 
the Bog and collect my head?!

00:08:03.330 --> 00:08:05.950
Such a fearsome man!

00:08:05.950 --> 00:08:07.880
<i>I feel like I'm being mocked.</i>

00:08:12.130 --> 00:08:15.390
H-He made it past the first plate!

00:08:17.890 --> 00:08:19.890
Th-The second, too?!

00:08:19.890 --> 00:08:22.660
He got through!

00:08:31.320 --> 00:08:34.650
<i>I can't put up with this farce any longer.</i>

00:08:34.650 --> 00:08:37.030
<i>I'll end it right—</i>

00:08:38.420 --> 00:08:40.040
<i>Tonegawa lets his guard down!</i>

00:08:40.040 --> 00:08:42.600
<i>He doesn't notice the trap laid by Ichijou!</i>

00:08:45.560 --> 00:08:47.000
It's futile, you see.

00:08:48.440 --> 00:08:51.510
No matter how many balls get 
through, they're all doomed.

00:08:52.210 --> 00:08:55.980
My three stages of plates are impassible.

00:08:55.980 --> 00:08:57.690
They're the true defense!

00:09:00.020 --> 00:09:04.040
<i>Surely enough, these plates... 
You can get close, but...</i>

00:09:04.680 --> 00:09:05.890
<i>The balls won't go in.</i>

00:09:06.450 --> 00:09:10.900
<i>I see. These plates, at least, 
are the real deal.</i>

00:09:11.670 --> 00:09:14.100
<i>This has actually gotten interesting!</i>

00:09:14.100 --> 00:09:15.900
<i>Tonegawa catches fire!</i>

00:09:17.910 --> 00:09:19.420
Go!

00:09:19.420 --> 00:09:22.410
<i>But, defying his inflamed 
sense of competition...</i>

00:09:22.790 --> 00:09:24.290
<i>He misses.</i>

00:09:24.290 --> 00:09:25.790
<i>And so does the next ball.</i>

00:09:26.250 --> 00:09:28.440
<i>And the next! And the one after!</i>

00:09:29.170 --> 00:09:31.920
<i>They sink without pause 
into the bottomless bog!</i>

00:09:36.070 --> 00:09:40.430
It's subtly and perfectly calculated. 
The perfect incline.

00:09:40.430 --> 00:09:44.440
Such is our impregnable, unbeatable plates.

00:09:45.060 --> 00:09:48.980
It's what has earned the 
Bog its demonic reputation!

00:09:48.980 --> 00:09:50.400
What do you think?

00:09:50.400 --> 00:09:53.690
Even Teiai's number two, Tonegawa-sensei,

00:09:53.690 --> 00:09:56.820
will find it a challenge beyond 
his reach! Don't you agree?

00:09:57.970 --> 00:09:59.820
I can't focus because you 
won't shut your trap!

00:09:59.820 --> 00:10:03.140
Oh, I'm ever so sorry, sir!

00:10:03.140 --> 00:10:04.330
Boss...

00:10:04.330 --> 00:10:05.720
I think it's time.

00:10:05.720 --> 00:10:07.060
I believe it is.

00:10:07.480 --> 00:10:10.230
Activate the Phoenix System!

00:10:10.230 --> 00:10:11.060
Yes, sir!

00:10:20.090 --> 00:10:20.840
<b>Psst...</b>

00:10:23.720 --> 00:10:24.850
What?!

00:10:26.850 --> 00:10:31.360
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:10:28.450 --> 00:10:31.360
The balls that fell into the holes 
are coming back, just like...

00:10:31.770 --> 00:10:33.640
a phoenix rising from the ashes!

00:10:34.680 --> 00:10:37.110
How can this be happening?!

00:10:37.590 --> 00:10:39.850
When was this done?! And how?!

00:10:39.850 --> 00:10:41.800
Who's responsible?!

00:10:42.280 --> 00:10:43.370
<i>It was obviously you.</i>

00:10:44.500 --> 00:10:46.740
But there's nothing we can do,

00:10:46.740 --> 00:10:49.610
because there's no evidence of foul play!

00:10:49.610 --> 00:10:51.500
<i>A total farce!</i>

00:10:51.500 --> 00:10:53.030
<i>A farce!</i>

00:10:55.530 --> 00:11:04.240
<i>Psst... Psst.... Psst...</i>

00:11:07.520 --> 00:11:09.810
It just... went in...

00:11:10.850 --> 00:11:12.250
Boss!

00:11:12.250 --> 00:11:13.440
It went in...

00:11:16.440 --> 00:11:19.950
The Bog... The Bog is crying!

00:11:19.950 --> 00:11:24.490
<i>Idiot. That would make anyone 
want to cry, even the Bog!</i>

00:11:24.920 --> 00:11:28.330
<i>In the end, everything went 
off without a hitch,</i>

00:11:28.330 --> 00:11:31.400
<i>and the game on the Bog 
concluded without incident.</i>

00:11:32.410 --> 00:11:34.520
<i>Rest easy, Tonegawa.</i>

00:11:35.290 --> 00:11:37.640
<i>Rest easy, Ichijou.</i>

00:11:38.740 --> 00:11:41.130
<i>Rest easy, Bog.</i>

00:11:41.940 --> 00:11:43.080
<i>Goodnight.</i>

00:11:44.890 --> 00:11:46.240
<i>The underground prison.</i>

00:11:46.240 --> 00:11:50.520
<i>The absolute bottom of the barrel. 
Teiai's subterranean labor camp.</i>

00:11:50.840 --> 00:11:52.810
That's 5,000 Perica for a beer, just 5,000!

00:11:52.810 --> 00:11:54.270
It's ice cold!

00:11:54.270 --> 00:11:56.240
1,400 perica for yakitori!

00:11:56.240 --> 00:11:58.020
It'll be 1,000 perica for a bag of snack mix!

00:11:58.390 --> 00:12:02.890
You won't find a better price! 
Come and get it while you can!

00:11:59.620 --> 00:12:03.530
<i>There are men who work hard at things 
other than their underground labor.</i>

00:12:03.530 --> 00:12:05.530
Yes, come right on up!

00:12:05.530 --> 00:12:07.530
You can get a tallboy for 6,000 perica!

00:12:07.950 --> 00:12:10.550
Now, now, don't push!

00:12:14.540 --> 00:12:17.970
<i>Ootsuki and Numakawa are released!</i>

00:12:19.300 --> 00:12:19.920
All right!

00:12:20.290 --> 00:12:22.880
We need to get going, Numakawa.

00:12:22.880 --> 00:12:25.390
Huh? We're not gonna relax a bit first?

00:12:25.390 --> 00:12:27.560
Idiot! Remember what I told you?

00:12:27.560 --> 00:12:30.690
This excursion is about refilling our stock!

00:12:30.690 --> 00:12:33.010
We don't have time to waste.

00:12:33.010 --> 00:12:35.590
Th-That's right! Sorry!

00:12:35.590 --> 00:12:36.680
<i>Indeed.</i>

00:12:36.680 --> 00:12:40.760
<i>The snacks that Ootsuki sells underground 
are, naturally, procured on the surface.</i>

00:12:41.370 --> 00:12:44.200
<i>In order to avoid spending 
multiple one-day passes,</i>

00:12:44.200 --> 00:12:47.200
<i>he purchases several months' 
worth in a single day.</i>

00:12:47.200 --> 00:12:50.410
<i>Given the massive amount of 
shopping, it takes a lot of time.</i>

00:12:50.410 --> 00:12:53.930
<b>Pizza Potato Chips</b>

00:12:50.410 --> 00:12:53.930
<b>Potato Chips</b>

00:12:50.410 --> 00:12:53.930
<b>Consomme Punch</b>

00:12:50.840 --> 00:12:52.730
<i>And it's about more than buying the goods.</i>

00:12:52.730 --> 00:12:57.460
<i>In order to keep his customers enticed, 
the stock is carefully selected.</i>

00:12:58.670 --> 00:13:02.320
The double consomme flavor 
is better than last time.

00:13:02.320 --> 00:13:04.990
Maybe we should drop the seaweed 
and salt flavor and go with this?

00:13:04.990 --> 00:13:07.640
I personally think the pizza 
chips are a possibility.

00:13:08.100 --> 00:13:11.840
<i>He makes his decisions based on 
his experience as a salesmen,</i>

00:13:11.840 --> 00:13:13.380
<i>but there's a lot to do.</i>

00:13:13.380 --> 00:13:18.390
<i>The usually fastidiously mellow Ootsuki 
is on pins and needles on this day!</i>

00:13:18.390 --> 00:13:20.440
<i>The men in black have their 
hands full transporting him!</i>

00:13:23.010 --> 00:13:25.300
We finished earlier than I thought.

00:13:25.300 --> 00:13:26.930
Want to go out for drinks?

00:13:26.930 --> 00:13:29.640
No, we're not done yet.

00:13:30.680 --> 00:13:32.450
What do you mean?

00:13:32.700 --> 00:13:37.830
I'm thinking about figuring 
out a new product to sell.

00:13:37.830 --> 00:13:39.480
A new product?

00:13:39.480 --> 00:13:44.240
Yeah. What we're doing right now 
is essentially moving contraband.

00:13:44.240 --> 00:13:47.260
We just sell the things that we buy.

00:13:47.260 --> 00:13:48.110
Right.

00:13:48.110 --> 00:13:50.100
You've heard, haven't you?

00:13:50.100 --> 00:13:55.600
Odagiri on Team C has 
recently begun selling, too.

00:13:55.600 --> 00:13:57.290
I saw it myself.

00:13:57.290 --> 00:14:01.110
Some guys from Team E were eating 
curry crackers and drinking Hoppy.

00:14:01.110 --> 00:14:03.480
We've never bought those before...

00:14:03.930 --> 00:14:09.240
Yeah. They call it Team C's Hoppy Meal, 
apparently, and it sells like crazy.

00:14:09.530 --> 00:14:19.250
<b>Psst... Psst...</b>

00:14:10.520 --> 00:14:12.170
The Hoppy Meal...

00:14:12.170 --> 00:14:15.820
We've taken chips and snack mix 
as far as they can go.

00:14:15.820 --> 00:14:19.250
I see now. I guess we do need new product.

00:14:19.250 --> 00:14:21.750
<b>DanQui</b>

00:14:19.250 --> 00:14:21.750
<b>The Home of Super Bargains</b>

00:14:19.740 --> 00:14:21.750
All right, let's go!

00:14:25.140 --> 00:14:26.090
Foreman!

00:14:26.090 --> 00:14:28.380
How about grilled sweet potatoes?

00:14:28.380 --> 00:14:31.850
We can buy some of the 
bruised ones at a discount,

00:14:31.850 --> 00:14:34.980
roast them up nice and fluffy, and sell them!

00:14:35.860 --> 00:14:37.360
It's not a bad idea.

00:14:37.360 --> 00:14:38.100
I know, right?

00:14:38.410 --> 00:14:40.350
But it's a bit weak.

00:14:41.350 --> 00:14:44.200
Warmer weather is on the way...

00:14:44.200 --> 00:14:46.360
And above all, the underground cafeteria

00:14:46.880 --> 00:14:49.860
has sweet potatoes in the 
miso soup sometimes.

00:14:51.080 --> 00:14:53.860
It's not exotic or luxurious enough.

00:14:54.370 --> 00:14:55.730
I get it...

00:14:55.730 --> 00:14:58.090
Sorry. I didn't think that one through.

00:14:58.090 --> 00:15:01.580
No, it's fine! We need to run 
through lots of ideas like that!

00:15:01.580 --> 00:15:07.140
There's no telling which one might be 
the inspiration for an explosive seller!

00:15:06.770 --> 00:15:12.430
<b>DanQui</b>

00:15:06.770 --> 00:15:12.430
<b>The Home of Super Bargains</b>

00:15:07.140 --> 00:15:10.410
<i>However, though they wandered the
store for several hours afterward,</i>

00:15:10.410 --> 00:15:12.420
<i>the two supposed brainstormers were found...</i>

00:15:13.140 --> 00:15:16.250
<i>doing nothing but enjoying themselves!</i>

00:15:17.160 --> 00:15:20.500
<i>They eventually retire for the day, 
without having come upon a winning idea,</i>

00:15:20.500 --> 00:15:22.950
<i>at a cheap business hotel.</i>

00:15:25.210 --> 00:15:27.940
<i>The next day, Ootsuki is 
still clinging to hope.</i>

00:15:28.770 --> 00:15:31.030
We've got an hour left...

00:15:31.030 --> 00:15:33.200
I don't think we're gonna find anything.

00:15:33.200 --> 00:15:35.350
<i>Damn it! There's gotta be something.</i>

00:15:35.350 --> 00:15:36.460
Foreman...

00:15:36.460 --> 00:15:39.400
<i>Something unexpected! 
Something cutting-edge!</i>

00:15:39.400 --> 00:15:40.820
Foreman!

00:15:41.460 --> 00:15:44.280
How about we take a break in here?

00:15:41.460 --> 00:15:44.920
<b>Unlimited Data (Fixed Rate)</b>

00:15:43.750 --> 00:15:45.460
<b>Unlimited Data (Fixed Rate)</b>

00:15:45.460 --> 00:15:48.710
We could have something sweet 
to wrap up our excursion.

00:15:49.140 --> 00:15:52.720
<i>A flash of inspiration 
brightens Ootsuki's day!</i>

00:15:54.580 --> 00:15:56.410
Rejoice, Numakawa!

00:15:57.060 --> 00:15:59.980
It's hit me, at the last possible second.

00:15:59.980 --> 00:16:03.650
Diabolical inspiration... A breakthrough!

00:16:05.400 --> 00:16:07.320
Man, I'm tired!

00:16:07.320 --> 00:16:09.030
I want a drink!

00:16:09.030 --> 00:16:11.030
<b>Perica Sales</b>

00:16:09.030 --> 00:16:11.030
<b>-Smokes
-Dried Squid
-Chips
-Sake
-Cold beer</b>

00:16:09.410 --> 00:16:11.030
Here we go! There's the snack cart!

00:16:13.030 --> 00:16:14.380
Beer and chips, please!

00:16:14.380 --> 00:16:15.570
I'll have a tallboy!

00:16:15.570 --> 00:16:19.790
All right, all right! Before we open up, 
the foreman has an announcement to make!

00:16:20.180 --> 00:16:21.690
Announcement?

00:16:21.290 --> 00:16:22.540
<b>Psst...</b>

00:16:22.540 --> 00:16:24.640
Well, gentlemen,

00:16:24.640 --> 00:16:29.550
first, I'd like to thank you 
for your daily patronage.

00:16:29.550 --> 00:16:31.320
Today, to show our gratitude,

00:16:31.320 --> 00:16:34.300
we have a deal that's downright 
dangerous to our margins!

00:16:34.300 --> 00:16:35.930
Dangerous?

00:16:34.430 --> 00:16:35.930
<b>Psst... Psst...</b>

00:16:36.440 --> 00:16:40.850
Essentially, we're ready to offer a new 
service that will give you a sizable discount

00:16:40.850 --> 00:16:42.010
on our regular prices.

00:16:42.010 --> 00:16:42.890
Isawa.

00:16:42.890 --> 00:16:43.940
Right.

00:16:45.110 --> 00:16:46.520
Here we go...

00:16:51.650 --> 00:16:52.910
That's...

00:16:52.910 --> 00:16:54.450
Snack mix?

00:16:54.450 --> 00:16:58.230
For 5,000 perica a month, 
you can have up to ten bags!

00:16:58.230 --> 00:17:01.450
It's what you've been waiting for... 
the all-you-can-eat snack mix service!

00:17:01.770 --> 00:17:04.460
I call it the Snack Mix Buffet!

00:17:04.460 --> 00:17:07.890
And we're starting it up today!

00:17:07.000 --> 00:17:07.890
<b>Psst...</b>

00:17:07.890 --> 00:17:10.230
S-Snack mix buffet?

00:17:10.230 --> 00:17:14.100
Wait, wait a second. A single bag 
of snack mix is 1,000 perica, so...

00:17:14.100 --> 00:17:16.330
If you had ten bags

00:17:16.330 --> 00:17:19.460
and it only cost 5,000, that means...

00:17:17.890 --> 00:17:18.660
<b>Psst...</b>

00:17:19.460 --> 00:17:22.840
It's half off! You're only paying 
half the price for the snack mix!

00:17:23.670 --> 00:17:25.730
<i>That's a good price!</i>

00:17:26.980 --> 00:17:29.720
It's a good deal, yeah...

00:17:29.720 --> 00:17:31.930
But you only get ten bags, right?

00:17:31.930 --> 00:17:34.760
That's not really all-you-can-eat, y'know?

00:17:35.530 --> 00:17:38.450
No need to worry about that.

00:17:38.450 --> 00:17:42.710
We've also got the real deal available...

00:17:39.590 --> 00:17:44.620
<b>All-You-Can-Eat Plan</b>

00:17:42.710 --> 00:17:45.410
An all-you-can-eat plan for snack mix!

00:17:44.620 --> 00:17:46.870
<b>All-You-Can-Eat Plan</b>

00:17:44.750 --> 00:17:46.870
<b>All the snack mix
you want for a</b>

00:17:44.750 --> 00:17:46.870
<b>A low monthly
cost of</b>

00:17:44.870 --> 00:17:46.870
<b><i>Five bags a month practically pays for itself...!</i></b>

00:17:45.080 --> 00:17:46.870
<b>Six-Month Contract</b>

00:17:45.120 --> 00:17:46.870
<b>Perica</b>

00:17:45.250 --> 00:17:46.870
<b>Best value!</b>

00:17:45.410 --> 00:17:47.120
<i>Psst... Psst...</i>

00:17:47.120 --> 00:17:50.120
It costs you the same 
per month as the buffet.

00:17:50.120 --> 00:17:53.590
The only difference is that it 
requires a six-month contract.

00:17:54.420 --> 00:17:55.510
I call it...

00:17:56.310 --> 00:17:58.760
Snack Mix Unlimited!

00:17:58.760 --> 00:18:00.160
<i>Psst...</i>

00:18:00.160 --> 00:18:04.770
If you eat five bags a month, you're making 
out like a bandit. A very special option.

00:18:05.490 --> 00:18:08.110
<i>Yet another good price!</i>

00:18:08.110 --> 00:18:09.770
And if you sign up for this plan...

00:18:10.520 --> 00:18:12.070
You can do this!

00:18:12.760 --> 00:18:15.440
You can practically drink the snack mix!

00:18:15.440 --> 00:18:18.170
Let me sign up! Gimme unlimited!

00:18:18.170 --> 00:18:18.570
Me, too!

00:18:18.570 --> 00:18:20.520
Over here!

00:18:18.570 --> 00:18:21.070
Okay, okay, one at a time!

00:18:21.070 --> 00:18:25.830
<i>Ultimately, on launch day, the majority 
of the team signs up under this plan.</i>

00:18:25.830 --> 00:18:29.840
<i>Even men from other teams end up signing up!</i>

00:18:29.840 --> 00:18:31.330
<i>It's a huge hit!</i>

00:18:31.330 --> 00:18:33.530
I love that you can eat as much as you want!

00:18:33.530 --> 00:18:35.430
Is this really going to work out?

00:18:35.430 --> 00:18:37.340
If they keep it up, we'll be in the red...

00:18:37.340 --> 00:18:39.270
It'll be perfectly fine.

00:18:39.270 --> 00:18:41.760
I give it ten days before 
they realize their limits.

00:18:42.950 --> 00:18:44.890
<i>And just as Ootsuki predicted...</i>

00:18:45.350 --> 00:18:47.350
You want some?

00:18:47.830 --> 00:18:51.510
Nah, I'm fine. I've still got plenty left.

00:18:51.510 --> 00:18:53.510
I'm tired of this, actually.

00:18:53.510 --> 00:18:55.360
I know, right?

00:18:55.360 --> 00:18:58.860
Huh? You want to cancel the plan?

00:18:59.210 --> 00:19:00.440
Y-Yeah.

00:19:00.440 --> 00:19:03.370
Okay. I understand. That's fine.

00:19:03.370 --> 00:19:05.230
Thank you so much!

00:19:05.230 --> 00:19:07.740
The thing is, the six months aren't up yet,

00:19:07.740 --> 00:19:10.370
so if you cancel now, 
it'll cost you 30,000 perica.

00:19:12.340 --> 00:19:14.770
It says it here in the contract, see?

00:19:14.770 --> 00:19:20.380
You can only cancel on one specific day, 
six months after you sign up.

00:19:17.380 --> 00:19:20.380
<b>In the event of failed payment, I agree to reimburse the contract holder</b>

00:19:17.380 --> 00:19:20.380
<b>I hereby agree to the above terms and wish to sign up for Snack Mix Unlimited.</b>

00:19:17.380 --> 00:19:20.380
Hirose Naomi

00:19:20.380 --> 00:19:21.630
That's tiny!

00:19:23.320 --> 00:19:24.670
<i>The subscribers try their best</i>

00:19:24.670 --> 00:19:29.140
<i>to avoid getting bored of the 
snack mix until their plan is up.</i>

00:19:29.140 --> 00:19:32.150
<i>This leads to a variety of 
snack mix recipes being suggested.</i>

00:19:32.150 --> 00:19:35.490
<i>Snack mix on rice. Snack mix in rice balls.</i>

00:19:35.490 --> 00:19:37.330
<i>Chikuwa stuffed with snack mix.</i>

00:19:37.330 --> 00:19:39.650
<i>Et cetera, et cetera!</i>

00:19:39.650 --> 00:19:44.660
<i>And most notable of them 
all is the snack mix ball!</i>

00:19:42.760 --> 00:19:44.660
<i>Ball...</i>

00:19:45.100 --> 00:19:48.320
<i>First, you separate the peanuts 
and the rice crackers...</i>

00:19:48.320 --> 00:19:52.460
<i>Then, after grinding up the crackers 
finely, you spray them with water.</i>

00:19:52.460 --> 00:19:54.800
<i>Then you form it like a meatball!</i>

00:19:54.800 --> 00:19:56.220
<i>After that...</i>

00:19:56.220 --> 00:19:59.850
<i>You sprinkle the crushed peanuts 
onto it, and it's finished!</i>

00:19:59.850 --> 00:20:02.930
<i>The snack mix ball!</i>

00:20:03.860 --> 00:20:05.200
This is actually pretty good!

00:20:05.200 --> 00:20:07.430
<i>A culinary boom occurs!</i>

00:20:08.650 --> 00:20:10.970
<i>And yet, after three days, 
it comes to a close.</i>

00:20:10.970 --> 00:20:13.610
<i>The amount of snack mix being 
consumed gradually eases off.</i>

00:20:13.610 --> 00:20:16.550
<i>After a month, it's down to zero.</i>

00:20:17.040 --> 00:20:20.440
<i>Ootsuki's big business plan 
goes off without a hitch!</i>

00:20:21.160 --> 00:20:23.510
Guys, today's the day!

00:20:23.510 --> 00:20:25.450
It's been so long...

00:20:25.450 --> 00:20:26.760
You get it, right?

00:20:26.760 --> 00:20:30.200
It's been six months since we signed 
up for Snack Mix Unlimited!

00:20:30.200 --> 00:20:33.830
If we don't cancel today, the 
subscription will automatically renew!

00:20:33.830 --> 00:20:36.210
Once we're done working, 
we need to cancel right away!

00:20:36.210 --> 00:20:37.960
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:20:36.650 --> 00:20:37.960
Yeah!

00:20:38.400 --> 00:20:41.090
<i>But on this day, Ootsuki...</i>

00:20:41.530 --> 00:20:45.860
<i>finds himself in Zoshigaya, 
absentmindedly enjoying an excursion.</i>

00:20:46.590 --> 00:20:50.100
No good! I can't find 
him anywhere! Foreman!

00:20:51.160 --> 00:20:55.060
Is this how you do business?!

00:20:55.060 --> 00:20:58.360
<i>Snack Mix unlimited automatically renews!</i>

00:20:58.360 --> 00:21:04.280
Huh... So Tezuka Osamu 
used to live around here?

00:21:04.760 --> 00:21:07.960
<i>Even when in the clutches 
of the underground prison,</i>

00:21:07.960 --> 00:21:11.340
<i>he seeks to maximize the enjoyment 
of his one-day excursions.</i>

00:21:11.340 --> 00:21:13.600
<i>From the bottom, he seeks the top!</i>

00:21:13.600 --> 00:21:19.050
<i>Where will Foreman Ootsuki's 
next one-day pass take him?</i>

00:22:54.890 --> 00:22:57.210
Next time, "Defamation."

00:22:55.990 --> 00:23:00.250
<b>Defamation</b>
